# Instructions for updating .env.local
# =====================================

Shamwari runs on Cloudflare Workers AI, reached through Cloudflare AI Gateway.
There is no Anthropic key and no Vercel AI Gateway key any more — if your
.env.local still has ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY, delete them.

## What you need

  CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=...      # required
  CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=...       # required
  CLOUDFLARE_AI_GATEWAY_ID=...   # optional but recommended

Without the first two, /api/ai/chat answers 503 ("AI service not configured")
and moderation reports ai_checked: false rather than silently passing content.

## How to get them

1. Account ID
   Cloudflare dashboard → Workers & Pages → Account details → Account ID.

2. API token
   https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens → Create Token → give it the
   "Workers AI" permission (read + run). Copy it once; Cloudflare will not show
   it again.

3. AI Gateway ID
   Cloudflare dashboard → AI → AI Gateway → create a gateway (e.g. "lingo").
   The id is the gateway's name. Requests then carry `cf-aig-gateway-id`, which
   is what gives you caching, per-gateway rate limits and a request log.
   If the gateway is set to "authenticated", also set
   CLOUDFLARE_AI_GATEWAY_TOKEN.

## Then

  - Save .env.local
  - Restart the dev server: stop it (Ctrl+C), then `npx expo start`

## For Production (Vercel)

Add the same variables to the Vercel project's environment variables:
https://vercel.com/nyuchitech/mukoko-lingo/settings/environment-variables

The app is still hosted on Vercel — only inference moved to Cloudflare.

## Changing model

The default is @cf/qwen/qwen3-30b-a3b-fp8. To try another Workers AI model,
set WORKERS_AI_MODEL to its @cf/... id; no code change or redeploy of the
function body is needed.
